   315	- **Script.** New script `gpu_experiments/run_b03_config_matched_erank_spike.py`, writing to `packets/B03/spikes/B03-SPIKE/{PLAN.md, VERDICT.json, runs.log}`.
   316	- **The existing `run_b03_rank16_erank_spike.py` does not conform and must not be used as evidence.** It draws tip vectors as independent Gaussian noise scaled by $L$, which violates F1–F4: no rigid-body coupling, no exact shells, no rank ≤ 8 structure. It trains on only 3 lengths, applies the stratified loss in both arms, and uses a pooled reference.
   317	- **Physics.** The generator is a **reduced surrogate**, not the V3 physics collector. A PASS is Candidate evidence only. Locking any claim beyond its Grade-1 algebra requires a re-run on D-B02-001's merged physics collector. Charter boundary 3 coverage metrics remain B02's responsibility and are not claimed here.
   318	
   319	### 5.2 Surrogate data generator
   320	
   321	- **Plant.** Single revolute link. Control at 50 Hz, with 4 semi-implicit substeps at 200 Hz. Inertia $J = I_{D,zz} + n_g^2J_{\mathrm{rotor}}$ with payload. Gravity, viscous and Coulomb friction, and spring-damper end stops. Capacity tier $C_0 \in \{3, 6, 9\}$ N·m, $S_{\max} = 1.25C_0$.
   322	- **Configurations.** 36 seeds with **distinct** $L_D$ on a log grid over $[0.08, 0.45]$ m, independently drawn payload mass and COM, tier $= $ seed mod 3; 4 stroke profiles per seed, giving 144 configurations.
   323	- **Scenes.** E0–E4 per D-B02-001: net-equilibrium sustained load with alternating sign, deterministic release edge plus recovery window, and a contact spring wall. The external-torque generator is causal.
   324	- **Behavior policy.** The D-B02-001 rule controller (scene-dependent feedforward gain $\kappa$; E3 = 1, E4 = 0) with random targets, plus 30% Ornstein–Uhlenbeck exploration.
   325	- **Volume.** Per configuration × scene: 600 training and 400 test transitions, 720,000 in total. Per configuration, 2,048 held-out outcomes at nominal $w_\sigma$ for rank statistics.
   326	- **Held-out geometry.** 8 of the 36 seeds (interior $L_D$ values, seed indices $\{2, 6, 11, 15, 20, 24, 29, 33\}$) are excluded from all training, including $\kappa$ selection and normalizer statistics. That is 32 held-out configurations.
   327	
   328	### 5.3 Ground-truth successor operators and B-limited error
   329	
   330	Training is μ-successor FB, i.e. evaluation of the behavior policy. This isolates outcome-representation capacity from actor learning; it is a limitation, see §5.8.
   331	
   332	- Per configuration, fit 256 k-means cells on test outcomes in $T_{\kappa^\star}$ space. Monte-Carlo the discounted occupancy from 256 anchor state-actions with horizon 150 and $\gamma = 0.98$, giving $M^{(k)}\in\mathbb R^{256\times256}$ as densities with respect to the cell masses of $\nu_k$.
   333	- **Configuration-matched error** $\varepsilon_k^{\mathrm{cm}}(B)$: the closed-form weighted least-squares residual of $M^{(k)}$ on cell-averaged $B$ features in $L^2(\nu_k)$, with a free left factor per row.
   334	- **Pooled error** $\varepsilon_k^{\mathrm{pool}}(B)$: the same, in $L^2(\nu)$ over the union of all $144 \times 256$ cells, with $M^{(k)}$ zero on other configurations' cells.
   335	- **Oracle floor** $\sum_{i>16}\lambda_i(W_k)$ per configuration, and the **theorem bound** $\sum_{i>16}\lambda_i(\bar W)$ for the pooled case.
   336	
   337	### 5.4 Training and arms
   338	
   339	All arms use V3's exact $\tilde B$ architecture with identical parameter count and $d_z = 16$. $F$ is training-only: a causal-$p$ compressor plus MLP $[512, 512] \to 16$. Target networks with $\tau = 0.005$, Adam at $10^{-4}$, 30,000 updates at batch size 1024, **3 seeds per arm**. The P0 ramp is simulated by drawing 50% E0 for the first 3,000 updates, to reproduce Issue #7.
